Privacy Policy – EH-Monitor Team Bot

Last updated: 27.9.2025




1. Introduction

This Privacy Policy explains how the EH-Monitor Team Bot (hereafter referred to as the Bot) handles and stores data when you use it on Discord servers.


---

2. Data We Collect

The Bot may collect and temporarily store the following information:

Discord IDs (user, server, channel, role) for configuration and permissions.

Ticket & command inputs (e.g., reasons for support tickets, server settings).

Configuration settings (channels, roles, embed messages, server preferences).



---

3. How We Use the Data

To provide the Bot’s functionality (ticket system, monitoring, team support).

To ensure only authorized users (staff/admins) can access certain features.

To improve stability, troubleshoot errors, and maintain the service.



---

4. Data Sharing

Data is never sold or shared with third parties.

Data is only accessible to the Bot owner/developers when necessary for support or debugging.



---

5. Data Storage & Retention

Data is stored securely in our systems or database.

Temporary information (such as ticket reasons) may be deleted automatically once the ticket or related process is closed.

You may request deletion of your server’s data at any time (see Section 7).



---

6. Security

We take reasonable steps to protect data from unauthorized access or misuse.
However, no system is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.


---

7. Your Rights

You may request deletion of stored data related to your server by contacting the Bot owner.

You may stop all data collection by removing the Bot from your server.



---

8. Changes to the Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated at any time. If significant changes are made, we will provide notice in the support server.


---

9. Contact

For questions, data deletion requests, or support, please use the official support server:
